PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key dispute remains EJR for ℓ=3 x-coalition S={1,2,3,8,9,10} (|S|=6, common {x1,x2,x3}) and ℓ=2 y-coalition T={4-7} (|T|=4, common {y4,y5,y6}). EJR existential: one i∈S with |A_i∩W|≥3, one j∈T with |A_j∩W|≥2.  

Round-3 consensus on lower bound: all agree min=2 (via {x1,x2,y4,y5,z1} satisfying S via z1 for voters 8-10 and T via two y's; dropping below two x's leaves S unsatisfied). Upper-bound constructions claiming 4 (e.g. {x1,x2,y1,z3,y4}) universally contain only one from {y4,y5,y6}, so every member of T receives |W∩A_j|=1, violating T quota. Valid W therefore requires ≥2 from {y4,y5,y6} + ≥2 from {x1,x2,x3}, exhausting four seats and capping |A1∩W| at 3 (via free seat = y1 or z3). Explicit max-3 witness {x1,x2,y1,y4,y5} meets both quotas existentially.  

Persistent A-side error: conflates existential requirement with allowing y1/z3 to substitute for a T-common y-candidate; definition supplies no such substitution. H now supported by majority of colleagues (2,3,4,6,8,10,12) with matching explicit committees; no new counter-examples or coalitions surfaced. Range therefore exactly [2,3] (choice H).}

